target: internal/docs/docs.go
verify: go test ./internal/docs/ -count=1 -run 'TestAnUnknownScriptDoesNotSwallowTheAttribution'
expect: --- FAIL: TestAnUnknownScriptDoesNotSwallowTheAttribution
why:    attribution picks the nearest script named on the line, but it must be the nearest one this directory CONTAINS. Without the guard a nearer mention of some other repo's tool wins, the flag is attributed to a script whose flags are unknown, and the real check is skipped in silence — the failure mode this package exists to prevent, reached through its own attribution step.
--- old
		if _, ok := flags[line[start:end]]; !ok {
			continue
		}
--- new
		if false {
			continue
		}
